{
  "about": "The shared roof-colour fixture (m3-design.md section 3; briefs M3-05 and M3-12), the seam between the pipeline's roofs step and the game's BuildingRoofs and BuildingLoader. World and area: the buildings fixture's (tests/shared/buildings_fixture/world.json, terrain.json: origin E 2650000 / N 1150000, height offset 500 m, area 'fixture' E 2650900-2651100, N 1149950-1150050). tests/shared/roofs_fixture/source.json is one sheet, 1249-42: the buildings fixture's eleven features unchanged (byte for byte, first) and six more, 12 to 17, all in the tile 2651-1149, which had no building: so the chunks 2650-1149, 2650-1150 and 2651-1150 are the buildings fixture's own bytes and 2651-1149 is new. The photo (photo.json, photo_<tile>.u8) is synthetic: 0.1 m source pixels on the national grid, only windows around the roofs, one file per 1 km tile; the colours are chosen so that every likely mistake listed under 'detectors' changes the named buildings (measured: each was run against this fixture). Everything under generated/ and the expected values were computed by design two independent ways (identical bytes): one with the repository's buildings functions, an exact Fraction scanline and Counter histograms, the other re-deriving the buildings in integers, numpy int64 edge functions and np.sort. generated/manifest.json is assembled by design in the manifest's final M3 shape (top level exactly buildings, photo, roofs, schema, surfaces, terrain, trees, world, world_sha256; this fixture's buildings and roofs blocks verbatim, every other block null; the text json.dumps(manifest, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) plus a newline): the wiring brief M3-13 must reproduce it byte for byte. roofs.json's computed_for: inputs_sha256 is the SHA-256 of json.dumps({'swissbuildings3d': <entry>, 'swissimage': <entry>}, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False) over datasets.lock.json's two entries, world_sha256 the world.json's. 'buildings' lists every selected building in chunk order with its expected roof; 'triangles' names triangles by their index in their chunk's triangle list (the file's order a, b, c) with their LV95 points and the file's float32 local positions: the game must draw each 'roof' one with its building's colour as vertex colour, each 'wall' one with the plaster placeholder, each 'neutral_roof' one with the neutral roof material.",
